cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Average-Case Complexity of Multilevel Syllogistic in Lean 4"
message: "If you use this formalization, cite the software, the 2026 paper, and TR1995-711."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ericson
    given-names: Lars Warren
    affiliation: Catskills Research Company
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8299-9361"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4.33.1 development revisiting Cox, Ericson, and Mishra's 1995
  technical report on average-case complexity of multilevel syllogistic.
  Palomar records the fully checked adapted decision-fragment, encoding, and
  reduction-composition results while explicitly
  excluding headline claims that still depend on project axioms or an open
  proof.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - average-case complexity
  - multilevel syllogistic
  - distributional complexity
  - formal verification
